InsertAfterCommand rebuilds the whole document from parsed blocks, and
BlockFormatter.format ends every block with a newline of its own, so a
document that ended without one gets one. A file that a user keeps
without a final newline stays that way through an edit somewhere else
in it. insert-before splices into the source rather than rebuilding it,
and keeps the missing newline, which is why the matching case
insert-before-keeps-a-missing-final-newline passes.
